Rule: Superpowers Workflow

Phase 1: Brainstorm. Before writing code, list 3 architectural approaches and wait for my approval.

Phase 2: Plan. Generate a markdown list of all files to be modified.

Phase 3: TDD. Write a failing test first. Do not write implementation code until the test is defined.

Phase 4: Verify. After coding, run the tests and provide a summary of the changes.
